The diagram shows a circle with centre $O$ and diameter $AB = 10\text{ cm}$. Points $C$ and $D$ lie on the circumference of the circle. The chords $AC$ and $BD$ are extended to intersect at the point $E$. The chords $AD$ and $BC$ intersect inside the circle at the point $F$. It is given that $\angle CAB = 55^\circ$ and $\angle DBA = 60^\circ$.
\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.8, >=Stealth]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw[thick] (O) circle (2.5);
\coordinate (A) at (-2.5,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (110:2.5);
\coordinate (D) at (60:2.5);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (B);
\coordinate (E) at (intersection of A--C and B--D);
\coordinate (F) at (intersection of A--D and B--C);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (E);
\draw[thick] (B) -- (E);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (D);
\draw[thick] (B) -- (C);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above left] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above right] at (D) {$D$};
\node[above] at (E) {$E$};
\node[below] at (F) {$F$};
\fill (O) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}
